        "content": "     1→[\n     2→  {\n     3→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n     4→    \"title\": \"Background Agents in Slack Integration\",\n     5→    \"description\": \"Cursor announced Background Agents in Slack integration, allowing users to launch agents directly from Slack by mentioning @Cursor. Agents can read threads, understand context, and create PRs without leaving the conversation. Also includes search in settings with Cmd/Ctrl+F, MCP progress notifications, dynamic tool registration, and roots support.\",\n     6→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n     7→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.sh/changelog\",\n     8→    \"date\": \"2026-04-10\",\n     9→    \"community_feedback\": [\n    10→      {\n    11→        \"quote\": \"Cursor background agents in Slack changed my workflow\",\n    12→        \"source\": \"Swizec Teller blog\",\n    13→        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n    14→      },\n    15→      {\n    16→        \"quote\": \"You say @cursor do my work in Slack and Agent is the same as what you see running in Cursor. An LLM loop that thinks, executes code, and edits files directly from Slack.\",\n    17→        \"source\": \"Swizec.com\",\n    18→        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n    19→      }\n    20→    ]\n    21→  },\n    22→  {\n    23→    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n    24→    \"title\": \"Version 2.1.105 - Enhanced Worktree Support and Security Fixes\",\n    25→    \"description\": \"Claude Code v2.1.105 added path parameter to EnterWorktree tool for switching into existing worktrees, PreCompact hook support, background monitor support for plugins, and /proactive alias for /loop. Includes critical security fixes: improved Bash tool permission handling, fixed stalled API streams with 5-minute timeout abort, and improved network error messages. Also improved /doctor layout, /config labels, and WebFetch to strip style/script contents.\",\n    26→    \"updateType\": \"feature_release\",\n    27→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/a