kground-color: #ffffff;\n   195→            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n   196→            padding: 1px 5px;\n   197→            font-size: 7pt;\n   198→            color: #828282;\n   199→            margin: 2px;\n   200→            border-radius: 2px;\n   201→        }\n   202→\n   203→        footer {\n   204→            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n   205→            padding: 15px 10px;\n   206→            text-align: center;\n   207→            border-top: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n   208→            font-size: 8pt;\n   209→            color: #828282;\n   210→        }\n   211→\n   212→        footer a {\n   213→            color: #828282;\n   214→        }\n   215→\n   216→        .stats {\n   217→            display: inline-block;\n   218→            margin: 0 10px;\n   219→        }\n   220→\n   221→        @media print {\n   222→            body {\n   223→                background-color: #ffffff;\n   224→            }\n   225→\n   226→            .column {\n   227→                break-inside: avoid;\n   228→            }\n   229→        }\n   230→\n   231→        .highlight {\n   232→            background-color: #ffffd0;\n   233→            padding: 0 2px;\n   234→        }\n   235→\n   236→        .github-stars {\n   237→            color: #ff6600;\n   238→            font-weight: bold;\n   239→        }\n   240→\n   241→        .product-hunt-points {\n   242→            color: #ff6600;\n   243→            font-weight: bold;\n   244→        }\n   245→    </style>\n   246→</head>\n   247→<body>\n   248→    <header>\n   249→        <div class=\"container\">\n   250→            <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report</h1>\n   251→            <div class=\"header-meta\">\n   252→                <span id=\"report-date\">2026-04-14</span> |\n   253→                <span>Daily Updates in AI-Powered Development Tools</span>\n   254→            </div>\n   255→        </div>\n   256→    </header>\n   257→\n   258→    <main class=\"container\">\n   259→        <div class=\"main-content\">\n   260→            <!-- New Products Column (40%) -->\n   261→            <section class=\"column\">\n   262→                <h2 class=\"column-header\">New Products</h2>\n   263→\n   264→                <div class=\"item\">\n   265→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   266→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent\" target=\"_blank\">hermes-agent</a>\n   267→                    </div>\n   268→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   269→                        Self-improving AI coding agent with closed learning loop that grows with usage. Features TUI interface, multi-platform support (Telegram, Discord, Slack), scheduled automations, and creates skills from experience.\n   270→                    </div>\n   271→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   272→                        <span class=\"github-stars\">61.9k GitHub stars (#7 globally)</span> |\n   273→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub Trending</span>\n   274→                    </div>\n   275→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Gained over 6,000+ stars in a single week during April 2026\"</div>\n   276→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   277→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   278→                        <span class=\"tag\">Self-improving</span>\n   279→                    </div>\n   280→                </div>\n   281→\n   282→                <div class=\"item\">\n   283→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   284→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/superhq\" target=\"_blank\">SuperHQ</a>\n   285→                    </div>\n   286→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   287→                        Run AI coding agents in real microVM sandboxes for secure, isolated execution environments. Provides 81-point score on Product Hunt and enables safe agent execution.\n   288→                    </div>\n   289→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   290→                        <span class=\"product-hunt-points\">81 Product Hunt points</span> |\n   291→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Product Hunt</span>\n   292→                    </div>\n   293→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   294→                        <span class=\"tag\">Infrastructure</span>\n   295→                        <span class=\"tag\">Security</span>\n   296→                        <span class=\"tag\">MicroVM</span>\n   297→                    </div>\n   298→                </div>\n   299→\n   300→                <div class=\"item\">\n   301→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   302→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/open-comet\" target=\"_blank\">Open Comet</a>\n   303→                    </div>\n   304→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   305→                        Autonomous AI browser agent for deep research and tasks. Navigates websites autonomously, clicks around, and handles research tasks. Positioned as \"Your browser just got an intern\".\n   306→                    </div>\n   307→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   308→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Product Hunt</span> |\n   309→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GrowthPigeon</span>\n   310→                    </div>\n   311→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Your browser just got an intern\"</div>\n   312→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   313→                        <span class=\"tag\">Browser Agent</span>\n   314→                        <span class=\"tag\">Research</span>\n   315→                        <span class=\"tag\">Automation</span>\n   316→                    </div>\n   317→                </div>\n   318→\n   319→                <div class=\"item\">\n   320→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   321→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/multica-ai/multica\" target=\"_blank\">multica</a>\n   322→                    </div>\n   323→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   324→                        Open-source managed agents platform that turns coding agents into real teammates. Features task assignment, autonomous execution tracking, reusable skills, unified runtimes, and multi-workspace support.\n   325→                    </div>\n   326→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   327→                        <span class=\"github-stars\">4,000+ GitHub stars in &lt;1 week</span> |\n   328→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub Trending</span>\n   329→                    </div>\n   330→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Someone just created the open-source version of Claude Managed Agents\"</div>\n   331→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   332→                        <span class=\"tag\">Agent Platform</span>\n   333→                        <span class=\"tag\">Team Management</span>\n   334→                        <span class=\"tag\">Open Source</span>\n   335→                    </div>\n   336→                </div>\n   337→\n   338→                <div class=\"item\">\n   339→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   340→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/thedotmack/claude-mem\" target=\"_blank\">claude-mem</a>\n   341→                    </div>\n   342→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   343→                        Claude Code plugin that automatically captures everything Claude does during coding sessions. Features persistent memory compression, 5 lifecycle hooks, MCP tools, SQLite + Chroma vector DB storage, and progressive disclosure.\n   344→                    </div>\n   345→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   346→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span> |\n   347→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Medium</span>\n   348→                    </div>\n   349→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"The plugin that turns Claude into a teammate\"</div>\n   350→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   351→                        <span class=\"tag\">Memory Plugin</span>\n   352→                        <span class=\"tag\">Vector DB</span>\n   353→                        <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n   354→                    </div>\n   355→                </div>\n   356→            </section>\n   357→\n   358→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Column (35%) -->\n   359→            <section class=\"column\">\n   360→                <h2 class=\"column-header\">Whitelist Updates</h2>\n   361→\n   362→                <div class=\"item\">\n   363→                    <span class=\"update-badge\">Feature Release</span>\n   364→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   365→                        <a href=\"https://codeium.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf v1.5.9</a>\n   366→                    </div>\n   367→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   368→                        Released version 1.5.9 with Gemini 2.5 Pro (Beta) support and fixes for Remote-SSH extension. Recent releases also include new Windsurf Tab experience, context improvements, Cascade auto-linter, and MCP server integration.\n   369→                    </div>\n   370→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   371→                        <span>📅 2025-03-25</span>\n   372→                    </div>\n   373→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   374→                        <span class=\"tag\">Gemini 2.5 Pro</span>\n   375→                        <span class=\"tag\">Remote-SSH</span>\n   376→                        <span class=\"tag\">MCP</span>\n   377→                    </div>\n   378→                </div>\n   379→\n   380→                <div class=\"item\">\n   381→                    <span class=\"update-badge\">Feature Release</span>\n   382→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   383→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/releases\" target=\"_blank\">Aider v0.86.0</a>\n   384→                    </div>\n   385→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   386→                        Added support for all GPT-5 models and Grok-4 via xAI and OpenRouter. Recent versions (0.83.0-0.86.0) added support for Gemini 2.5 Pro, DeepSeek V3, new /context command, co-authored-by attribution, and 130 new languages with linter support.\n   387→                    </div>\n   388→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   389→                        <span>📅 2025-04-14</span>\n   390→                    </div>\n   391→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   392→                        <span class=\"tag\">GPT-5</span>\n   393→                        <span class=\"tag\">Grok-4</span>\n   394→                        <span class=\"tag\">DeepSeek V3</span>\n   395→                        <span class=\"tag\">Multi-language</span>\n   396→                    </div>\n   397→                </div>\n   398→\n   399→                <div class=\"item\">\n   400→                    <span class=\"update-badge\">Minor Release</span>\n   401→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   402→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases\" target=\"_blank\">Continue v1.3.38</a>\n   403→                    </div>\n   404→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   405→                        Released v1.3.38-vscode with config.yaml fixes, session history filtering by workspace directory, and .continue/configs support. Recent updates include ClawRouter provider for cost-optimized routing, JetBrains remote config sync improvements, and Gemini 3 tool support.\n   406→                    </div>\n   407→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   408→                        <span>📅 2025-04-14</span>\n   409→                    </div>\n   410→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   411→                        <span class=\"tag\">Config</span>\n   412→                        <span class=\"tag\">ClawRouter</span>\n   413→                        <span class=\"tag\">Gemini 3</span>\n   414→                        <span class=\"tag\">JetBrains</span>\n   415→                    </div>\n   416→                </div>\n   417→            </section>\n   418→\n   419→            <!-- Technical Insights Column (25%) -->\n   420→            <section class=\"column\">\n   421→                <h2 class=\"column-header\">Technical Insights</h2>\n   422→\n   423→                <div class=\"item\">\n   424→                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   425→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   426→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">LLMs and the Peril of Laziness Lost</a>\n   427→                    </div>\n   428→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   429→                        Bryan Cantrill argues that LLMs inherently lack the virtue of laziness - work costs nothing to an LLM, so they don't optimize for future time or develop crisp abstractions.\n   430→                    </div>\n   431→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   432→                        <span class=\"author\">Bryan Cantrill</span> | 📅 2026-04-13\n   433→                    </div>\n   434→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   435→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-assisted-programming</span>\n   436→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">llms</span>\n   437→                    </div>\n   438→                </div>\n   439→\n   440→                <div class=\"item\">\n   441→                    <span class=\"insight-type tutorial\">Tutorial</span>\n   442→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   443→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Gemma 4 E2B Audio Transcription</a>\n   444→                    </div>\n   445→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   446→                        Simon shared a recipe for transcribing audio files on macOS using the 10.28GB Gemma 4 E2B model with MLX and mlx-vlm.\n   447→                    </div>\n   448→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   449→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> | 📅 2026-04-12\n   450→                    </div>\n   451→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   452→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">gemma</span>\n   453→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">mlx</span>\n   454→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">speech-to-text</span>\n   455→                    </div>\n   456→                </div>\n   457→\n   458→                <div class=\"item\">\n   459→                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   460→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   461→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Growing Gap in AI Capability Understanding</a>\n   462→                    </div>\n   463→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   464→                        Andrej Karpathy tweeted about the growing gap in understanding of AI capability based on access points and domains.\n   465→                    </div>\n   466→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   467→                        <span class=\"author\">Andrej Karpathy</span> | 📅 2026-04-10\n   468→                    </div>\n   469→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   470→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">openai</span>\n   471→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">chatgpt</span>\n   472→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">llms</span>\n   473→                    </div>\n   474→                </div>\n   475→\n   476→                <div class=\"item\">\n   477→                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   478→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   479→                        <a href=\"https://medium.com/neuralnotions/andrej-karpathy-stopped-using-ai-to-write-code-hes-using-it-to-build-a-second-brain-instead-cddceadc5df5\" target=\"_blank\">Karpathy's Shift from AI Coding to Second Brain</a>\n   480→                    </div>\n   481→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   482→                        Andrej Karpathy reportedly stopped using AI to write code and is instead focusing on using LLMs to build a 'Second Brain' - a personal knowledge base system.\n   483→                    </div>\n   484→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   485→                        <span class=\"author\">Andrej Karpathy</span> | 📅 2026-04-11\n   486→                    </div>\n   487→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   488→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">llm</span>\n   489→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">knowledge-base</span>\n   490→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">personal-ai</span>\n   491→                    </div>\n   492→                </div>\n   493→\n   494→                <div class=\"item\">\n   495→                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   496→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   497→                        <a href=\"https://thenewstack.io/karpathy-says-developers-have-ai-psychosis-everyone-else-is-next/\" target=\"_blank\">Karpathy's 'AI Psychosis' Warning</a>\n   498→                    </div>\n   499→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   500→                        Andrej Karpathy warned about 'AI psychosis' among developers, saying he 'started to lose his ability to code' due to over-reliance on AI programming tools.\n   501→                    </div>\n   502→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   503→                        <span class=\"author\">Andrej Karpathy</span> | 📅 2026-04-11\n   504→                    </div>\n   505→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   506→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-assisted-programming</span>\n   507→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">developer-tools</span>\n   508→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">code-atrophy</span>\n   509→                    </div>\n   510→                </div>\n   511→\n   512→                <div class=\"item\">\n   513→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   514→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   515→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Meta's Muse Spark Model Launch</a>\n   516→                    </div>\n   517→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   518→                        Meta announced Muse Spark, their first model release since Llama 4 almost exactly a year ago. Features interesting tool capabilities and reasoning features.\n   519→                    </div>\n   520→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   521→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> | 📅 2026-04-08\n   522→                    </div>\n   523→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   524→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">llm-release</span>\n   525→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">meta</span>\n   526→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">llm-tool-use</span>\n   527→                    </div>\n   528→                </div>\n   529→\n   530→                <div class=\"item\">\n   531→                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   532→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   533→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic's Project Glasswing</a>\n   534→                    </div>\n   535→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   536→                        Anthropic didn't release their latest model, Claude Mythos, to the public. Instead, they made it available to a very restricted set of preview partners under Project Glasswing.\n   537→                    </div>\n   538→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   539→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> | 📅 2026-04-07\n   540→                    </div>\n   541→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   542→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">anthropic</span>\n   543→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">llm-release</span>\n   544→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-security-research</span>\n   545→                    </div>\n   546→                </div>\n   547→\n   548→                <div class=\"item\">\n   549→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   550→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   551→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">GLM-5.1: 754B Parameter Model</a>\n   552→                    </div>\n   553→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   554→                        Chinese AI lab Z.ai's GLM-5.1 is a 754B parameter, 1.51TB MIT-licensed model. Demonstrated sophisticated understanding of SVG, CSS transforms, and animation issues.\n   555→                    </div>\n   556→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   557→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> | 📅 2026-04-07\n   558→                    </div>\n   559→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   560→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">llm-release</span>\n   561→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">glm</span>\n   562→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">svg</span>\n   563→                    </div>\n   564→                </div>\n   565→\n   566→                <div class=\"item\">\n   567→                    <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n   568→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   569→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Google AI Edge Gallery</a>\n   570→                    </div>\n   571→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   572→                        Google released AI Edge Gallery, an official app for running Gemma 4 models (E2B and E4B sizes) directly on iPhone. The 2.54GB E2B model is fast and useful.\n   573→                    </div>\n   574→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   575→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> | 📅 2026-04-06\n   576→                    </div>\n   577→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   578→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">google</span>\n   579→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">local-llms</span>\n   580→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">gemma</span>\n   581→                    </div>\n   582→                </div>\n   583→\n   584→                <div class=\"item\">\n   585→                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   586→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   587→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Eight Years of Wanting, Three Months of Building</a>\n   588→                    </div>\n   589→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   590→                        Lalit Maganti's deep dive into building syntaqlite, high-fidelity devtools for SQLite. The project took 8 years of thinking but only 3 months of building, thanks to AI.\n   591→                    </div>\n   592→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   593→                        <span class=\"author\">Lalit Maganti</span> | 📅 2026-04-05\n   594→                    </div>\n   595→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   596→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">sqlite</span>\n   597→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-assisted-programming</span>\n   598→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n   599→                    </div>\n   600→                </div>\n   601→            </section>\n   602→        </div>\n   603→    </main>\n   604→\n   605→    <footer>\n   606→        <div class=\"container\">\n   607→            <div class=\"stats\">\n   608→                <strong>5</strong> New Products\n   609→            </div>\n   610→            <div class=\"stats\">\n   611→                <strong>3</strong> Whitelist Updates\n   612→            </div>\n   613→            <div class=\"stats\">\n   614→                <strong>10</strong> Technical Insights\n   615→            </div>\n   616→            <div style=\"margin-top: 10px;\">\n   617→                <a href=\"#\">Archives</a> |\n   618→                <a href=\"#\">About</a> |\n   619→                <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a> |\n   620→                <a href=\"#\">GitHub</a>\n   621→            </div>\n   622→            <div style=\"margin-top: 5px;\">\n   623→                Generated on 2026-04-14 | Agentic Coding Research Report\n   624→            </div>\n   625→        </div>\n   626→    </footer>\n   627→</body>\n   628→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
