-04-13\n   288→                    </div>\n   289→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Gained over 6,000+ stars in a single week during April 2026\"</div>\n   290→                </div>\n   291→\n   292→                <div class=\"item\">\n   293→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   294→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/posts/superhq\" target=\"_blank\">SuperHQ</a>\n   295→                    </div>\n   296→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   297→                        Run AI coding agents in real microVM sandboxes for secure, isolated execution environments. Provides 81-point score on Product Hunt and enables safe agent execution.\n   298→                    </div>\n   299→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   300→                        <span class=\"badge\">AI coding infrastructure</span>\n   301→                        <span class=\"badge\">Product Hunt</span>\n   302→                        <span class=\"badge\">Security</span>\n   303→                        <br>\n   304→                        Released: 2026-04-13\n   305→                    </div>\n   306→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Promoted product on Product Hunt with 81 points\"</div>\n   307→                </div>\n   308→\n   309→                <div class=\"item\">\n   310→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   311→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/multica-ai/multica\" target=\"_blank\">multica</a>\n   312→                    </div>\n   313→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   314→                        Open-source managed agents platform that turns coding agents into real teammates. Features task assignment, autonomous execution tracking, reusable skills, unified runtimes, and multi-workspace support. Gained 4,000+ GitHub stars in less than a week.\n   315→                    </div>\n   316→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   317→                        <span class=\"badge\">AI agent platform</span>\n   318→                        <span class=\"badge\">GitHub</span>\n   319→                        <span class=\"badge\">Trending</span>\n   320→                        <span class=\"badge\">LinkedIn</span>\n   321→                        <br>\n   322→                        Released: 2026-04-08\n   323→                    </div>\n   324→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Someone just created the open-source version of Claude Managed Agents\"</div>\n   325→                </div>\n   326→\n   327→                <div class=\"item\">\n   328→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   329→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/thedotmack/claude-mem\" target=\"_blank\">claude-mem</a>\n   330→                    </div>\n   331→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   332→                        Claude Code plugin that automatically captures everything Claude does during coding sessions. Features persistent memory compression, 5 lifecycle hooks, MCP tools, SQLite + Chroma vector DB storage, and progressive disclosure. Consolidated 267 commits and 39 releases in v10.x era.\n   333→                    </div>\n   334→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   335→                        <span class=\"badge\">AI memory plugin</span>\n   336→                        <span class=\"badge\">GitHub</span>\n   337→                        <span class=\"badge\">Medium</span>\n   338→                        <br>\n   339→                        Released: 2026-04-04\n   340→                    </div>\n   341→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"The plugin that turns Claude into a teammate\"</div>\n   342→                </div>\n   343→            </section>\n   344→\n   345→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section (35%) -->\n   346→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   347→                <h2>Product Updates</h2>\n   348→\n   349→                <div class=\"item\">\n   350→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   351→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code v2.1.105</a>\n   352→                    </div>\n   353→                    <span class=\"update-type\">Feature Release</span>\n   354→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   355→                        Enhanced worktree support with path parameter for switching into existing worktrees, PreCompact hook support, background monitor support for plugins, and /proactive alias for /loop. Critical security fixes: improved Bash tool permission handling, fixed stalled API streams with 5-minute timeout abort.\n   356→                    </div>\n   357→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   358→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Security</span>\n   359→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Worktree</span>\n   360→                        <br>\n   361→                        Updated: 2026-04-13\n   362→                    </div>\n   363→                </div>\n   364→\n   365→                <div class=\"item\">\n   366→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   367→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor - Background Agents in Slack</a>\n   368→                    </div>\n   369→                    <span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span>\n   370→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   371→                        Launch agents directly from Slack by mentioning @Cursor. Agents can read threads, understand context, and create PRs without leaving the conversation. Also includes search in settings with Cmd/Ctrl+F, MCP progress notifications, dynamic tool registration.\n   372→                    </div>\n   373→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   374→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Slack Integration</span>\n   375→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Automation</span>\n   376→                        <br>\n   377→                        Updated: 2026-04-10\n   378→                    </div>\n   379→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"You say @cursor do my work in Slack and Agent is the same as what you see running in Cursor\"</div>\n   380→                </div>\n   381→\n   382→                <div class=\"item\">\n   383→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   384→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot - April 2026 Updates</a>\n   385→                    </div>\n   386→                    <span class=\"update-type\">Feature Release</span>\n   387→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   388→                        Copilot SDK in public preview, Copilot cloud agent with research/plan/code capabilities, Copilot CLI now supports BYOK and local models, organization runner controls for cloud agent, and usage metrics now identify active/passive code review users.\n   389→                    </div>\n   390→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   391→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">SDK</span>\n   392→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Cloud Agent</span>\n   393→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">BYOK</span>\n   394→                        <br>\n   395→                        Updated: 2026-04-08\n   396→                    </div>\n   397→                </div>\n   398→\n   399→                <div class=\"item\">\n   400→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   401→                        <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini CLI v0.37.0</a>\n   402→                    </div>\n   403→                    <span class=\"update-type\">Feature Release</span>\n   404→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   405→                        Dynamic sandbox expansion and worktree support for Linux and Windows. Introduced 'Chapters' narrative flow for better session structure, and enhanced browser agent with persistent sessions and dynamic tool discovery.\n   406→                    </div>\n   407→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   408→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Sandbox</span>\n   409→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Worktree</span>\n   410→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Browser Agent</span>\n   411→                        <br>\n   412→                        Updated: 2026-04-08\n   413→                    </div>\n   414→                </div>\n   415→\n   416→                <div class=\"item\">\n   417→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   418→                        <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf - Adaptive Model Router</a>\n   419→                    </div>\n   420→                    <span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span>\n   421→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   422→                        Adaptive model router intelligently selects the best model for each task. Updated model picker with pricing context, prompt cache timer, and token counts in response cards. Fixed bug with adaptive router preventing model switching after first request.\n   423→                    </div>\n   424→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   425→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Model Router</span>\n   426→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Optimization</span>\n   427→                        <br>\n   428→                        Updated: 2026-04-07\n   429→                    </div>\n   430→                </div>\n   431→\n   432→                <div class=\"item\">\n   433→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   434→                        <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/2026\" target=\"_blank\">Devin - PR Resumption</a>\n   435→                    </div>\n   436→                    <span class=\"update-type\">Feature</span>\n   437→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   438→                        PR resumption capability allowing agents to take over existing pull requests across sessions. Includes sidebar collapse state persistence, improved PR loading without GitHub integration, repository branch dropdown enhancements, and mobile responsive layout improvements.\n   439→                    </div>\n   440→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   441→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">PR Resumption</span>\n   442→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Mobile</span>\n   443→                        <br>\n   444→                        Updated: 2026-04-01\n   445→                    </div>\n   446→                </div>\n   447→\n   448→                <div class=\"item\">\n   449→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   450→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/releases\" target=\"_blank\">Aider v0.86.0</a>\n   451→                    </div>\n   452→                    <span class=\"update-type\">Feature Release</span>\n   453→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   454→                        Added support for all GPT-5 models and Grok-4 via xAI and OpenRouter. Also added support for Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite, new /context command for identifying files to edit, co-authored-by attribution enabled by default, and /commit-language option.\n   455→                    </div>\n   456→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   457→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">GPT-5</span>\n   458→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Grok-4</span>\n   459→                        <br>\n   460→                        Updated: 2025-04-14\n   461→                    </div>\n   462→                </div>\n   463→\n   464→                <div class=\"item\">\n   465→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   466→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases\" target=\"_blank\">Continue v1.3.38</a>\n   467→                    </div>\n   468→                    <span class=\"update-type\">Minor Release</span>\n   469→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   470→                        Config.yaml fixes, session history filtering by workspace directory, .continue/configs support, JetBrains remote config sync improvements, and Gemini 3 tool support with suffix stripping and thought_signature features.\n   471→                    </div>\n   472→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   473→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Config</span>\n   474→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Workspace</span>\n   475→                        <br>\n   476→                        Updated: 2025-04-14\n   477→                    </div>\n   478→                </div>\n   479→\n   480→                <div class=\"item\">\n   481→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   482→                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">Codex CLI v0.104.0</a>\n   483→                    </div>\n   484→                    <span class=\"update-type\">Feature Release</span>\n   485→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   486→                        WS_PROXY/WSS_PROXY environment support for websocket proxying, and app-server v2 now emits notifications when threads are archived/unarchived. Fixed Ctrl+C/Ctrl+D to cleanly exit during cwd-change prompts.\n   487→                    </div>\n   488→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   489→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">WebSocket</span>\n   490→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Notifications</span>\n   491→                        <br>\n   492→                        Updated: 2026-02-18\n   493→                    </div>\n   494→                </div>\n   495→            </section>\n   496→\n   497→            <!-- Technical Insights Section (25%) -->\n   498→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   499→                <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n   500→\n   501→                <div class=\"item\">\n   502→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   503→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/14/anthropic-co-founder-confirms-company-briefed-trump-administration-on-mythos/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic Briefed Trump Administration on Mythos</a>\n   504→                    </div>\n   505→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   506→                        Anthropic co-founder confirmed briefing the Trump administration on their Mythos model. Reports suggest Trump officials may be encouraging banks to test Anthropic's Mythos model.\n   507→                    </div>\n   508→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   509→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Sarah Perez</span>\n   510→                        <span class=\"badge\">TechCrunch</span>\n   511→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">anthropic</span>\n   512→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">ai-policy</span>\n   513→                        <br>\n   514→                        2026-04-14\n   515→                    </div>\n   516→                </div>\n   517→\n   518→                <div class=\"item\">\n   519→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   520→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/14/google-adds-ai-skills-to-chrome-to-help-you-save-favorite-workflows/\" target=\"_blank\">Google Adds AI Skills to Chrome</a>\n   521→                    </div>\n   522→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   523→                        Google announced AI Skills for Chrome, a new feature that helps users save and automate favorite workflows, integrating AI capabilities directly into browser functionality.\n   524→                    </div>\n   525→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   526→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Sarah Perez</span>\n   527→                        <span class=\"badge\">TechCrunch</span>\n   528→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">google</span>\n   529→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">chrome</span>\n   530→                        <br>\n   531→                        2026-04-14\n   532→                    </div>\n   533→                </div>\n   534→\n   535→                <div class=\"item\">\n   536→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   537→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/14/how-vibe-coding-app-anything-is-rebuilding-after-getting-booted-from-the-app-store-twice/\" target=\"_blank\">Vibe-Coding App Anything Rebuilding</a>\n   538→                    </div>\n   539→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   540→                        The vibe-coding app Anything is rebuilding after getting booted from the App Store twice, highlighting challenges faced by AI-powered coding applications in app store ecosystems.\n   541→                    </div>\n   542→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   543→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">Ivan Mehta</span>\n   544→                        <span class=\"badge\">TechCrunch</span>\n   545→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">vibe-coding</span>\n   546→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">app-store</span>\n   547→                        <br>\n   548→                        2026-04-14\n   549→                    </div>\n   550→                </div>\n   551→\n   552→                <div class=\"item\">\n   553→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   554→                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com\" target=\"_blank\">Show HN: LangAlpha - Claude Code for Wall Street</a>\n   555→                    </div>\n   556→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   557→                        A new project called LangAlpha asks 'what if Claude Code was built for Wall Street?' This specialized AI coding assistant targets financial domain use cases.\n   558→                    </div>\n   559→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   560→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">ginlix-ai</span>\n   561→                        <span class=\"badge\">Hacker News</span>\n   562→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">finance</span>\n   563→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">claude-code</span>\n   564→                        <br>\n   565→                        2026-04-14\n   566→                    </div>\n   567→                </div>\n   568→\n   569→                <div class=\"item\">\n   570→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   571→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/kontext-dev\" target=\"_blank\">Show HN: Kontext CLI - Credential Broker</a>\n   572→                    </div>\n   573→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   574→                        Kontext CLI is a credential broker for AI coding agents written in Go. It addresses the security challenge of managing credentials and API keys when working with autonomous AI coding systems.\n   575→                    </div>\n   576→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   577→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">kontext-dev</span>\n   578→                        <span class=\"badge\">Hacker News</span>\n   579→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">security</span>\n   580→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">go</span>\n   581→                        <br>\n   582→                        2026-04-14\n   583→                    </div>\n   584→                </div>\n   585→\n   586→                <div class=\"item\">\n   587→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   588→                        <a href=\"https://thetypicalset.com\" target=\"_blank\">The M×N Problem of Tool Calling</a>\n   589→                    </div>\n   590→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   591→                        Technical analysis of the M×N (model × tool) problem in tool calling with open-source models, exploring combinatorial challenges of making multiple tools work across multiple AI models efficiently.\n   592→                    </div>\n   593→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   594→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">remilouf</span>\n   595→                        <span class=\"badge\">Hacker News</span>\n   596→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">llm-tool-use</span>\n   597→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">open-source</span>\n   598→                        <br>\n   599→                        2026-04-14\n   600→                    </div>\n   601→                </div>\n   602→\n   603→                <div class=\"item\">\n   604→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   605→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Bryan Cantrill on LLMs and Laziness</a>\n   606→                    </div>\n   607→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   608→                        Bryan Cantrill argues that LLMs inherently lack the virtue of laziness - work costs nothing to an LLM, so they don't optimize for future time or develop crisp abstractions.\n   609→                    </div>\n   610→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   611→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">Bryan Cantrill</span>\n   612→                        <span class=\"badge\">Simon Willison</span>\n   613→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">llms</span>\n   614→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">software-engineering</span>\n   615→                        <br>\n   616→                        2026-04-13\n   617→                    </div>\n   618→                </div>\n   619→\n   620→                <div class=\"item\">\n   621→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   622→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Gemma 4 E2B Audio Transcription</a>\n   623→                    </div>\n   624→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   625→                        Simon shared a recipe for transcribing audio files on macOS using the 10.28GB Gemma 4 E2B model with MLX and mlx-vlm.\n   626→                    </div>\n   627→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   628→                        <span class=\"badge tutorial\">Simon Willison</span>\n   629→                        <span class=\"badge tutorial\">gemma</span>\n   630→                        <span class=\"badge tutorial\">mlx</span>\n   631→                        <span class=\"badge tutorial\">speech-to-text</span>\n   632→                        <br>\n   633→                        2026-04-12\n   634→                    </div>\n   635→                </div>\n   636→\n   637→                <div class=\"item\">\n   638→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   639→                        <a href=\"https://medium.com/neuralnotions/andrej-karpathy-stopped-using-ai-to-write-code-hes-using-it-to-build-a-second-brain-instead-cddceadc5df5\" target=\"_blank\">Karpathy's Shift from AI Coding to Second Brain</a>\n   640→                    </div>\n   641→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   642→                        Andrej Karpathy reportedly stopped using AI to write code and is instead focusing on using LLMs to build a 'Second Brain' - a personal knowledge base system.\n   643→                    </div>\n   644→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   645→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">Andrej Karpathy</span>\n   646→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">llm</span>\n   647→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">knowledge-base</span>\n   648→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">obsidian</span>\n   649→                        <br>\n   650→                        2026-04-11\n   651→                    </div>\n   652→                </div>\n   653→\n   654→                <div class=\"item\">\n   655→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   656→                        <a href=\"https://thenewstack.io/karpathy-says-developers-have-ai-psychosis-everyone-else-is-next/\" target=\"_blank\">Karpathy's 'AI Psychosis' Warning</a>\n   657→                    </div>\n   658→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   659→                        Andrej Karpathy warned about 'AI psychosis' among developers, saying he 'started to lose his ability to code' due to over-reliance on AI programming tools.\n   660→                    </div>\n   661→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   662→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">Andrej Karpathy</span>\n   663→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">ai-assisted-programming</span>\n   664→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">code-atrophy</span>\n   665→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">vibe-coding</span>\n   666→                        <br>\n   667→                        2026-04-11\n   668→                    </div>\n   669→                </div>\n   670→\n   671→                <div class=\"item\">\n   672→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   673→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Karpathy: Growing Gap in AI Capability</a>\n   674→                    </div>\n   675→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   676→                        Andrej Karpathy tweeted about the growing gap in understanding of AI capability based on access points and domains, highlighting differences between free and paid AI models.\n   677→                    </div>\n   678→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   679→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">Andrej Karpathy</span>\n   680→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">openai</span>\n   681→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">chatgpt</span>\n   682→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">llms</span>\n   683→                        <br>\n   684→                        2026-04-10\n   685→                    </div>\n   686→                </div>\n   687→\n   688→                <div class=\"item\">\n   689→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   690→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Meta's Muse Spark Model Launch</a>\n   691→                    </div>\n   692→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   693→                        Meta announced Muse Spark, their first model release since Llama 4 almost exactly a year ago. It's hosted (not open weights) and currently in private API preview, with interesting tool capabilities.\n   694→                    </div>\n   695→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   696→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Simon Willison</span>\n   697→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">meta</span>\n   698→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">llm-release</span>\n   699→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">llm-tool-use</span>\n   700→                        <br>\n   701→                        2026-04-08\n   702→                    </div>\n   703→                </div>\n   704→\n   705→                <div class=\"item\">\n   706→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   707→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic's Project Glasswing</a>\n   708→                    </div>\n   709→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   710→                        Anthropic didn't release their latest model, Claude Mythos, to the public. Instead, they made it available to a very restricted set of preview partners under Project Glasswing.\n   711→                    </div>\n   712→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   713→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">Simon Willison</span>\n   714→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">anthropic</span>\n   715→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">llm-release</span>\n   716→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">ai-security-research</span>\n   717→                        <br>\n   718→                        2026-04-07\n   719→                    </div>\n   720→                </div>\n   721→\n   722→                <div class=\"item\">\n   723→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   724→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">GLM-5.1: 754B Parameter Model</a>\n   725→                    </div>\n   726→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   727→                        Chinese AI lab Z.ai's GLM-5.1 is a 754B parameter, 1.51TB MIT-licensed model. Simon tested its ability to generate SVG with CSS animations, demonstrating sophisticated understanding.\n   728→                    </div>\n   729→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   730→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Simon Willison</span>\n   731→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">glm</span>\n   732→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">llm-release</span>\n   733→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">svg</span>\n   734→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">css</span>\n   735→                        <br>\n   736→                        2026-04-07\n   737→                    </div>\n   738→                </div>\n   739→            </section>\n   740→        </main>\n   741→\n   742→        <footer>\n   743→            <p>\n   744→                Report generated by <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code\">Agent Code Daily</a> -\n   745→                Powered by <a href=\"https://claude.com/claude-code\">Claude Agent SDK</a>\n   746→            </p>\n   747→            <p style=\"margin-top: 5px;\">\n   748→                <a href=\"#\">View Source</a> |\n   749→                <a href=\"#\">Previous Reports</a> |\n   750→                <a href=\"#\">Subscribe</a>\n   751→            </p>\n   752→            <p style=\"margin-top: 5px;\">\n   753→                Generated on 2026-04-14 | Agentic Coding Research Report\n   754→            </p>\n   755→        </footer>\n   756→    </div>\n   757→</body>\n   758→</html>"
