          "-                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Google AI Edge Gallery</a>",
          "+                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Karpathy: Growing Gap in AI Capability</a>",
          "                     </div>",
          "                     <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "-                        Google released AI Edge Gallery, an official app for running Gemma 4 models (E2B and E4B sizes) directly on iPhone. The 2.54GB E2B model is fast and useful.",
          "+                        Andrej Karpathy tweeted about the growing gap in understanding of AI capability based on access points and domains, highlighting differences between free and paid AI models.",
          "                     </div>",
          "                     <div class=\"item-meta\">",
          "-                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> | 📅 2026-04-06",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">Andrej Karpathy</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">openai</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">chatgpt</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">llms</span>",
          "+                        <br>",
          "+                        2026-04-10",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"topics\">",
          "-                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">google</span>",
          "-                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">local-llms</span>",
          "-                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">gemma</span>",
          "+                </div>",
          "+",
          "+                <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "+                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Meta's Muse Spark Model Launch</a>",
          "                     </div>",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "+                        Meta announced Muse Spark, their first model release since Llama 4 almost exactly a year ago. It's hosted (not open weights) and currently in private API preview, with interesting tool capabilities.",
          "+                    </div>",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-meta\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Simon Willison</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge technical\">meta</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge technical\">llm-release</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge technical\">llm-tool-use</span>",
          "+                        <br>",
          "+                        2026-04-08",
          "+                    </div>",
          "                 </div>",
          " ",
          "                 <div class=\"item\">",
          "-                    <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>",
          "                     <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "-                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Eight Years of Wanting, Three Months of Building</a>",
          "+                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic's Project Glasswing</a>",
          "                     </div>",
          "                     <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "-                        Lalit Maganti's deep dive into building syntaqlite, high-fidelity devtools for SQLite. The project took 8 years of thinking but only 3 months of building, thanks to AI.",
          "+                        Anthropic didn't release their latest model, Claude Mythos, to the public. Instead, they made it available to a very restricted set of preview partners under Project Glasswing.",
          "                     </div>",
          "                     <div class=\"item-meta\">",
          "-                        <span class=\"author\">Lalit Maganti</span> | 📅 2026-04-05",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">Simon Willison</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">anthropic</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">llm-release</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">ai-security-research</span>",
          "+                        <br>",
          "+                        2026-04-07",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"topics\">",
          "-                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">sqlite</span>",
          "-                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-assisted-programming</span>",
          "-                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">vibe-coding</span>",
          "+                </div>",
          "+",
          "+                <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "+                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">GLM-5.1: 754B Parameter Model</a>",
          "                     </div>",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "+                        Chinese AI lab Z.ai's GLM-5.1 is a 754B parameter, 1.51TB MIT-licensed model. Simon tested its ability to generate SVG with CSS animations, demonstrating sophisticated understanding.",
          "+                    </div>",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-meta\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Simon Willison</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge technical\">glm</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge technical\">llm-release</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge technical\">svg</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"badge technical\">css</span>",
          "+                        <br>",
          "+                        2026-04-07",
          "+                    </div>",
          "                 </div>",
          "             </section>",
          "-        </div>",
          "-    </main>",
          "+        </main>",
          " ",
          "-    <footer>",
          "-        <div class=\"container\">",
          "-            <div class=\"stats\">",
          "-                <strong>5</strong> New Products",
          "-            </div>",
